sheet-fn-help-pmt = Constant loan payment from rate, periods, present value, optional future value and payment type (0 end, 1 start).
sheet-fn-help-ipmt = Interest part of a payment for a chosen period; accepts rate, period, total periods, present value and optional future value and type.
sheet-fn-help-ppmt = Principal part of a payment for a chosen period; same arguments as IPMT.
sheet-fn-help-fv = Future value of an investment with constant payments: rate, periods, payment, optional present value and type.
sheet-fn-help-pv = Present value of an investment with constant payments: rate, periods, payment, optional future value and type.
sheet-fn-help-rate = Interest rate per period that balances a loan: periods, payment, present value, optional future value, type and guess.
sheet-fn-help-nper = Number of periods needed to repay a loan: rate, payment, present value, optional future value and type.
sheet-fn-help-npv = Net present value of a series of cash flows discounted at one rate; the first flow is discounted one period.
sheet-fn-help-irr = Internal rate of return of a series of cash flows, found by iteration; an optional guess helps convergence.
sheet-fn-help-mirr = Modified internal rate of return using a finance rate for negative flows and a reinvestment rate for positive flows.
sheet-fn-help-xirr = Internal rate of return for uneven dates: cash flows, their serial dates and an optional guess.
sheet-fn-help-xnpv = Net present value for uneven dates: discount rate, cash flows and their serial dates.
sheet-fn-help-sln = Straight-line depreciation per period from cost, salvage value and useful life.
sheet-fn-help-syd = Sum-of-the-years-digits depreciation for a chosen period from cost, salvage, life and period.
sheet-fn-help-db = Declining-balance depreciation for a period, with an optional first-year month count.
sheet-fn-help-ddb = Double-declining-balance depreciation, capped by salvage value; factor defaults to two.
sheet-fn-help-effect = Effective annual rate from a nominal rate and the number of compounding periods per year.
sheet-fn-help-nominal = Nominal annual rate from an effective rate and the number of compounding periods per year.
sheet-fn-help-networkdays = Count of working days between two dates, inclusive, excluding weekends and optional holidays.
sheet-fn-help-networkdays-intl = NETWORKDAYS with a custom weekend mask: a number code or a seven-character string where 1 marks a weekend day.
sheet-fn-help-workday = Date before or after a number of working days from a start date, skipping weekends and optional holidays.
sheet-fn-help-workday-intl = WORKDAY with a custom weekend mask given as a number code or a seven-character string.
sheet-fn-help-eomonth = Last day of the month before or after a number of months from a start date.
sheet-fn-help-edate = Date the same number of months before or after a start date, keeping the day when possible.
sheet-fn-help-yearfrac = Fraction of a year between two dates using a day-count basis: 0 US, 1 actual, 2 actual/360, 3 actual/365, 4 European.
sheet-fn-help-weeknum = Week number of a date; return type 1 starts on Sunday, 2 on Monday and 21 uses ISO weeks.
sheet-fn-help-isoweeknum = ISO 8601 week number of a date, where week 1 contains the first Thursday of the year.
sheet-fn-help-datedif = Difference between two dates in days, months, years or the partial units MD, YM and YD.
sheet-fn-help-correl = Pearson correlation coefficient of two numeric arrays.
sheet-fn-help-slope = Slope of the linear regression line fitted to known y and known x arrays.
sheet-fn-help-intercept = Intercept of the linear regression line fitted to known y and known x arrays.
sheet-fn-help-forecast-linear = Predicted y for a given x from a linear regression over known y and known x arrays.
sheet-fn-help-stdev-s = Sample standard deviation of a numeric array.
sheet-fn-help-stdev-p = Population standard deviation of a numeric array.
sheet-fn-help-var-s = Sample variance of a numeric array.
sheet-fn-help-var-p = Population variance of a numeric array.
sheet-fn-help-mode-sngl = Most frequently occurring value in a numeric array; returns #N/A when none repeats.
sheet-fn-help-norm-dist = Normal distribution value at x: cumulative probability when cumulative is true, density otherwise.
sheet-fn-help-norm-inv = Inverse of the normal cumulative distribution for a probability, with mean and standard deviation.
sheet-fn-help-textjoin = Join text values with a delimiter, optionally ignoring empty values.
sheet-fn-help-concat = Concatenate text values without a delimiter.
sheet-fn-help-numbervalue = Convert locale-formatted text to a number using explicit decimal and group separators.
sheet-fn-help-sum = Add numbers in a range or list; non-numeric text produces #VALUE!.
sheet-fn-help-average = Arithmetic mean of numbers in a range or list.
sheet-fn-help-count = Count numeric values in a list; text is not counted as zero.
sheet-fn-help-countif = Count values in a range that match a criterion such as >10 or a text value.
sheet-fn-help-if = Return one value when a condition is true and another when it is false.
sheet-fn-help-iferror = Return a fallback when a value is any Excel error, otherwise return the value.
sheet-fn-help-ifna = Return a fallback only when a value is #N/A; other errors propagate.
sheet-fn-help-iserror = Test whether a value is any Excel error.
sheet-fn-help-isna = Test whether a value is specifically #N/A.
sheet-fn-help-max = Largest number in a range or list.
sheet-fn-help-min = Smallest number in a range or list.
sheet-fn-help-round = Round a number to a given number of decimal digits.
